In this tutorial, we will create a harmless program that can mimic the functionality of malware or ransomware. This program will be able to encrypt files, but it will not be able to decrypt them. This means that the program will be able to lock files, but it will not be able to unlock them. This is similar to how ransomware works, but this program will not be able to demand payment in exchange for the decryption key.

Step 1: Create a new project in Visual Studio. Choose C# as the programming language and a console application as the project type.

Step 2: In the Program.cs file, add the following code:
```
using System;
using System.IO;

class Program
{
    static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        Console.WriteLine("Enter the path to the file you want to lock:");
        string filePath = Console.ReadLine();
        LockFile(filePath);
    }

    static void LockFile(string filePath)
    {
        if (File.Exists(filePath))
        {
            string fileExtension = Path.GetExtension(filePath);
            string fileWithoutExtension = Path.GetFileNameWithoutExtension(filePath);
            string lockedFile = Path.Combine(Path.GetDirectoryName(filePath), fileWithoutExtension + "_locked" + fileExtension);

            File.Copy(filePath, lockedFile);
            File.Delete(filePath);
        }
        else
        {
            Console.WriteLine("The file does not exist.");
        }
    }
}
```
This code will create a copy of the file and then delete the original file. The copy will have the same name as the original file, but with "_locked" added to the end.

Step 3: Run the program. Enter the path to a file when prompted. The program will create a copy of the file and then delete the original file. The copy will have the same name as the original file, but with "_locked" added to the end.

Step 4: The file is now locked. You can verify this by trying to open the file. The file will not be able to be opened because it has been deleted.

Step 5: You can unlock the file by renaming it back to its original name. For example, if the file was originally named "example.txt" and it was locked, you can unlock it by renaming it back to "example.txt".
